third_party/mesa-26.2.1/src/util/xxhash.h | BSD-2-Clause | xxHash: the file header says "BSD 2-Clause License"
driver/src/pvr/generated/csbgen/rogue/*.h | MIT | output of Mesa csbgen from Mesa XML (MIT text in the file, NOTICE 1a); check.sh regenerates it, so no edit
driver/src/v3d/generated/util/format/u_format_gen.h | MIT | output of Mesa u_format_table.py (MIT text in the file, NOTICE 1b); check.sh regenerates it
driver/src/v3d/generated/v3d_packet_v42_pack.h | MIT | output of Mesa gen_pack_header.py from v3d_packet.xml (UPSTREAM generated:, NOTICE 1b); check.sh regenerates it
include/KHR/khrplatform.h | MIT | Khronos header; the licence text in the file is the MIT text (NOTICE 6)
driver/rust/src/soc/imx8mp/regs.rs | generated-ok | NXP register data (BSD-3-Clause, NOTICE 10) through our Apache-2.0 generator
src/pvr/csbgen.rs | generated-ok | bindgen over Mesa csbgen output (MIT, NOTICE 1a) via yakogl-tools
driver/src/pvr/generated/csbgen_wrap.c | generated-ok | bindgen over Mesa csbgen output (MIT, NOTICE 1a) via yakogl-tools
#
# ---- Origins settled on 2026-10-26 (docs/release/license-audit.md,
# "Remaining findings"). These were `undecided` rows; each now names the
# source its licence was read from. No `undecided` row is left: a file of
# unknown origin leaves the tree (owner rule, 2026-10-26).
tools/shaders/femtovg/*.frag | MIT OR Apache-2.0 | femtovg 0.26.0 main-fs.glsl as its program.rs assembles it, with our nostd patch (NOTICE 8); verify_variants.py rebuilds all 36 from the crate byte for byte
tools/shaders/femtovg/*.vert | MIT OR Apache-2.0 | femtovg 0.26.0 main-vs.glsl as its program.rs assembles it (NOTICE 8)
tools/shaders/offarm/* | MIT OR Apache-2.0 | femtovg fill_color.nodiscard.frag plus our steps, written by tools/gen_offarm.py (NOTICE 8)
tools/cts/testdata/wedge-shaders/* | Apache-2.0 | dEQP shaders.algorithm.{hsl_to_rgb,rgb_to_hsl}_*: the template of es2fShaderAlgorithmTests.cpp, VK-GL-CTS 93bca01 (NOTICE 5), rebuilt byte for byte
tools/pvr/km/fwinit-step7.diff | Apache-2.0 | diff -u of two of our km records (object tables of our C and our Rust FWIF setup)
tools/pvr/rgxstart/rgxstart.diff | Apache-2.0 | diff -u of two register-access traces our harnesses recorded; check.sh compares it byte for byte
tools/pvr/rgxstart/*.trace | Apache-2.0 | register offsets and values our recording sys_io logged (record_main.sh, rgxlayer_check.c): measurements, no DDK text
tools/mali/isa-ref/board-2026-10-18.mesa-26.2.1.txt | Apache-2.0 AND MIT | Mesa 26.2.1 va_disasm (mnemonics from its ISA.xml, MIT, NOTICE 1e3) over the words of our board run; written by tools/mali/va_disasm_ref.sh
driver/src/display/golden-linux-2026-09-21.txt | Apache-2.0 | register values read on our board with mmio_rd while Linux drove the panel (2026-09-21): hardware state, no driver text
website/og-image.png | Apache-2.0 | written by tools/website-og-image.py (byte for byte; its tEXt chunks carry the SPDX lines)
#
# Test data that is read byte for byte by a test, a gate row or a self-test:
# a header would change what the test checks. Output of our own tools and
# board runs, or inputs written for this project.
tests/fixtures/deqp_random_dead_cube/* | Apache-2.0 | shaders from the dEQP random generator (VK-GL-CTS is Apache-2.0, NOTICE 5); the source hash is a test input
tools/cts/testdata/* | Apache-2.0 | self-test inputs and expected outputs of tools/cts; compared byte for byte
tools/mali/testdata/* | Apache-2.0 | probe shaders written for this project and their disassembly / traces; compared byte for byte
tools/mali/panthor/uapi_pins.expected | Apache-2.0 | expected output of the panthor UAPI pin check
tools/mali/isa-ref/board-2026-10-18.txt | Apache-2.0 | disassembly of our board run
tools/mali/board-dump/*.txt | Apache-2.0 | records of our board runs
tools/hostharness/glmark2/testdata/* | Apache-2.0 | fixtures of the host harness's report tools: logs and reports the harness wrote
tools/shaders/known-uncompilable-v3d.txt | Apache-2.0 | list of our own shader table
driver/rust/tests/gm-record/* | Apache-2.0 | recorded page lists and SNVS captures of our board runs
#
# Our scripts and test that name Mesa's vendored files in their header (the
# audit reads the UPSTREAM `generated:` paths as their generator). Their own
# licence is the header's; NOTICE 1a/1b states Apache-2.0 AND MIT for what they
# produce. Header not touched here: whether it should say `AND MIT` is the owner's.
src/mali/genxml/mesa_tests.rs | generated-ok | our test over Mesa's generated packers (NOTICE 1b)
tools/mali/gen_isa_rs.py | generated-ok | our generator over Mesa's ISA XML (MIT, NOTICE 1b)
tools/mali/gen_pack_rs.py | generated-ok | our generator over Mesa's genxml (MIT, NOTICE 1b)
